{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"/*\\n    This program solves Laplace's equation on a regular 2D grid using simple Jacobi iteration.\\n\\n    The stencil calculation stops at convergence or the iteration limit.\\n*/\\n#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <time.h>\\n#include <sys/time.h>\\n\\n#define CONV_THRESHOLD 1.0e-5f // threshold of convergence\\n\\n// matrix to be solved\\ndouble **grid;\\n\\n// auxiliary matrix\\ndouble **new_grid;\\n\\nstatic double *grid_storage;\\nstatic double *new_grid_storage;\\n\\n// size of each side of the grid\\nint size;\\nint iter_max_num;\\n\\n// return the absolute value of a number\\ndouble absolute(double num){\\n    if(num < 0)\\n        return -1.0 * num;\\n    return num;\\n}\\n\\n// allocate contiguous storage with row-pointer views\\nvoid allocate_memory(){\\n    size_t n = (size_t)size;\\n    grid = (double **) malloc(n * sizeof(double *));\\n    new_grid = (double **) malloc(n * sizeof(double *));\\n    grid_storage = (double *) malloc(n * n * sizeof(double));\\n    new_grid_storage = (double *) malloc(n * n * sizeof(double));\\n\\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\\n        grid[i] = grid_storage + (size_t)i * n;\\n        new_grid[i] = new_grid_storage + (size_t)i * n;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// initialize the grid\\nvoid initialize_grid(){\\n    int center = size / 2;\\n    int linf = center - (size / 10);\\n    int lsup = center + (size / 10);\\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++){\\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; j++){\\n            // inicializa região de calor no centro do grid\\n            if ( i >= linf && i <= lsup && j >= linf && j <= lsup)\\n                grid[i][j] = 100;\\n            else\\n                grid[i][j] = 0;\\n            // Both time levels must retain the original fixed boundaries.\\n            new_grid[i][j] = grid[i][j];\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// save the grid in a file\\nvoid save_grid(){\\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\\n        for(int j = 0; j < size; j++){\\n            fprintf(stdout, \\\"%lf \\\", grid[i][j]);\\n        }\\n        fprintf(stdout, \\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nstatic inline int update_row(double *restrict destination,\\n                             const double *restrict above,\\n                             const double *restrict current,\\n                             const double *restrict below){\\n    int changed = 0;\\n    for(int j = 1; j < size - 1; j++){\\n        double value = 0.25 * (current[j+1] + current[j-1] +\\n                               above[j] + below[j]);\\n        destination[j] = value;\\n        double errorCurrent = absolute(value - current[j]);\\n        changed |= (errorCurrent > CONV_THRESHOLD);\\n    }\\n    return changed;\\n}\\n\\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]){\\n    fscanf(stdin, \\\"%d\\\", &size);\\n    fscanf(stdin, \\\"%d\\\", &iter_max_num);\\n\\n    int hasError = 1;\\n    int iter = 0;\\n\\n    // allocate memory to the grid (matrix)\\n    allocate_memory();\\n\\n    // set grid initial conditions\\n    initialize_grid();\\n\\n    while(hasError && iter < iter_max_num){\\n        if(iter_max_num - iter == 1){\\n            // An unpaired final iteration uses the auxiliary time level.\\n            hasError = 0;\\n            for(int i = 1; i < size - 1; i++){\\n                hasError |= update_row(new_grid[i], grid[i-1],\\n                                       grid[i], grid[i+1]);\\n            }\\n            double **temporary = grid;\\n            grid = new_grid;\\n            new_grid = temporary;\\n            iter++;\\n        }else{\\n            int firstError = 0;\\n            int secondError = 0;\\n\\n            // Pipeline two sweeps, keeping the second one a row behind.\\n            // After first-step row i is complete, original row i-1 is\\n            // no longer needed and can hold its second-step result.\\n            for(int i = 1; i < size - 1; i++){\\n                firstError |= update_row(new_grid[i], grid[i-1],\\n                                         grid[i], grid[i+1]);\\n                if(i > 1){\\n                    secondError |= update_row(grid[i-1], new_grid[i-2],\\n                                              new_grid[i-1], new_grid[i]);\\n                }\\n            }\\n            if(size > 2){\\n                secondError |= update_row(grid[size-2], new_grid[size-3],\\n                                          new_grid[size-2], new_grid[size-1]);\\n            }\\n\\n            iter++;\\n            if(!firstError){\\n                // Discard the speculative second step if the first converged.\\n                double **temporary = grid;\\n                grid = new_grid;\\n                new_grid = temporary;\\n                hasError = 0;\\n            }else{\\n                iter++;\\n                hasError = secondError;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    //save the final grid in file\\n    save_grid();\\n\\n    free(grid_storage);\\n    free(new_grid_storage);\\n    free(grid);\\n    free(new_grid);\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/laplace_seq.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"Pipelining two Jacobi sweeps one row apart should improve temporal locality by consuming intermediate rows while cache-resident and eliminating whole-grid copy passes.\",\"notes\":\"Preserves stencil addition order, per-iteration convergence, fixed boundaries, and odd iteration limits. Not executed or measured.\",\"research\":{\"queries\":[],\"urls\":[]},\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Allocate contiguous matrix storage with row-pointer views and identical fixed boundaries in both buffers.\",\"Fuse pairs of sweeps using a one-row-lag traversal that safely writes second-step results into the original grid.\",\"Track convergence separately for both steps, selecting the intermediate grid if the first step converges; handle an unpaired final step with a pointer swap.\",\"Use a restrict-qualified row kernel with an integer OR convergence reduction.\"]}"}}
